==Battleground==
*1 [[Trolly Blogger]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Those Guys]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.2 seconds<sup>2f~6f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] (1,400%) spawn, delay 0.07~0.33 seconds<sup>2f~10f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Those Guys]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**30 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.2 seconds<sup>2f~6f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[Those Guys]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**50 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**100 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage isn't super challenging, and is definitely the easiest level in Dead End Night.

Aside from that, it can take a while. Bring area attackers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Brainwashed Sexy Legs Cat]] to clear out the endless peons. When the boss arrives, let him get close to your base. Use [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]] to damage him. Your best chance to damage him is after the Cat Cannon is fired. You should win after a while. If you have [[Awakened Bahamut Cat|Awakened Bahamut]], he can destroy the base before Nyandam can finish his attack. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can also help destroy large groups of Those Guys and Trolly Bloggers, and kill the base quickly if your cats are already there.

